  "summary": "Malicious code in grommatts (PyPI)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (35e98ba166154b4fd5d6672409ef3a28cd02da19168beba0c32d2a88a39fb2d1)\nThe package contains no detected install-time network activity, no credential or filesystem harvesting, no shell execution of fetched content, and no lifecycle hooks performing outbound I/O. No attacker-controlled destinations, no reads of installer secret paths, and no persistence mechanisms are present in the shipped source.\n\n## Source: kam193 (19b2f82a5bea773c2f47efa91e029f047a508d4c8d117eb102728056d0ac5bc3)\nThis campaign consists of similar loader packages, which provide executing code from a given URL. While they do not contain the malicious payload and the usage remains unknown, they are clearly a coordinated campaign to place multiple deceptive ways to load malicious code.\n\n\n---\n\nCategory: MALICIOUS - The campaign has clearly malicious intent, like infostealers.\n\n\nCampaign: 2026-10-voice-synthesis-profiles\n\n\nReasons (based on the campaign):\n\n\n - Downloads and executes a remote malicious script.\n\n\n - other\n",
